# Jev 1.13 — findings by Glyph Cluster

- Source: TypeSafe AI (`jev-1.13`, via OpenCode `opencode/jev-1.13`)
- Date: 2026-11-11 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Jev 1.13
- **Short description:** TypeSafe AI's System One typed-decision model (not a generative chat LLM) that evaluates state against structured questions (noul/choice/score) and returns values/probabilities for routing, triage, and guardrail workflows.
- **Provider / access:** TypeSafe API (`POST /v1/systemone`) and OpenCode Console inference endpoint (`https://opencode.ai/inference/systemone/v1/systemone`) for `jev-1.13` / `jev-1.13-free`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Versioned model documented by TypeSafe; release date and knowledge cutoff not stated as conventional LLM fields in sources reviewed.
- **IDs:** `jev-1.13.0` (TypeSafe model ID), aliases/context vary; OpenCode exposes `jev-1.13` and `jev-1.13-free`.
- **Context window:** 64K per request (32K state + 32K question) by default; 262K opt-in via header per TypeSafe docs (per local meta/docs).
- **Modalities:** Text, JSON, or array state in; typed decision outputs out (noul/choice/score). No text generation, no image/audio/video generation; Jev family supports image input in newer versions but Jev 1.13 question types listed as choice/score/noul in TypeSafe models docs.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** $0.042 per 1M input tokens; output free (per TypeSafe/OpenCode docs). Free limited-time slot `jev-1.13-free` available on OpenCode.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary System One decision model; not a conventional autoregressive text LLM.

